WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.698
Can a court give a Governor

2
00:00:01.698 --> 00:00:03.361
a deadline to decide on a bill?

3
00:00:03.589 --> 00:00:06.197
Article 200 gives the Governor options:

4
00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.427
assent, withhold assent,

5
00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.092
or reserve the bill for the

6
00:00:10.092 --> 00:00:10.558
President.

7
00:00:11.129 --> 00:00:13.053
It sets no fixed time limit.

8
00:00:13.414 --> 00:00:15.719
In April 2025, a two-judge

9
00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:17.492
bench set timelines,

10
00:00:17.674 --> 00:00:20.087
and treated ten Tamil Nadu

11
00:00:20.087 --> 00:00:23.057
bills as having received assent.

12
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.440
The President then sought

13
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.400
the Court's opinion under

14
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.341
Article 143.

15
00:00:28.688 --> 00:00:32.284
In November 2025, five judges advised:

16
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:34.344
courts cannot fix timelines,

17
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.636
and there is no deemed assent.

18
00:00:37.086 --> 00:00:38.758
But a Governor cannot sit

19
00:00:38.758 --> 00:00:40.296
on a bill indefinitely.

20
00:00:40.615 --> 00:00:42.378
For prolonged inaction, a

21
00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:44.352
court may direct a decision.

22
00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:45.821
No fixed clock.

23
00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:47.842
But no endless wait.

24
00:00:48.253 --> 00:00:48.804
Your turn.

25
00:00:49.029 --> 00:00:50.229
Which Article covers the

26
00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:51.580
Governor's assent to bills?
